            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0380" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/233: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-22T13:00:00-03:00">September 22, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 22—12:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. Department’s telegram No. 111, September 21, 6 p.m. The Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs will recommend to President Vargas that coffee be donated to the Spanish
                    refugees on condition that the difficulties which have recently arisen again in
                    intensified form in conjunction with the refugees in the Brazilian Embassy at
                    Madrid (my despatches 861, September 5 and 887, September 13<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d385-f1"/>) be adjusted. The Brazilian Government desires to remove
                    those refugees from territory dominated by the Barcelona Government.</p>
                <p>Aranha added that the Franco government is “buying” coffee for the regions
                    occupied by him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
